Body:
@fwang pushed d80e86b four hours after this was filed: per-model privacy table for all 17 Go models, 14 stay "Not used / 0 days", DeepSeek V4 Flash is the only "Used / No agreement", Grok and GPT Luna flag their 30 days with footnotes citing x.ai and OpenAI's own docs. Good progress.

This morning commit 2df47ee said "Your data will not be used for model training." in every locale. 9 hours later, we get a privacy table where DeepSeek V4 Flash has "Used" for model training. One of those two statements is wrong about the same prompt on the same day.

Remaining questions are: which upstream serves which model, the server-side telemetry pipeline, and confirmation that no Go or Zen paid provider has prompt-content storage.

+1 from the Omarchy side (a Linux desktop distro): our bar widget already renders Claude Code and Codex usage with rolling/weekly/monthly meters (`usagePercent`, reset countdown, alarm at 90%). OpenCode's local `opencode.db` gives us token totals, but not the plan windows — so the widget can't show what actually stops the next prompt.

A single REST endpoint like `/go/usage` returning `{ rollingUsage: { usagePercent, resetInSec, limit }, weeklyUsage: {...}, monthlyUsage: {...} }` would unblock us (and dashboards/CLI tools) with zero browser login — same auth as `/zen/v1/models`.

@thdxr is this on the roadmap? Happy to help spec it or test an early version — 37signals' DHH pointed at this exact need when we upstreamed an OpenCode provider, so there's real consumer demand.
